    "answer": {
      "short": "Join $(7{:}10\\text{ am},0)$, $(7{:}30\\text{ am},2)$, $(7{:}50\\text{ am},17)$, $(8{:}00\\text{ am},17)$ and $(8{:}35\\text{ am},25)$ with straight segments. Distances are in kilometres from home.",
      "worked": "At Burwood station: 7:30 am, 2 km from home.\n\nAt Epping: 7:50 am, $2+15=17$ km from home.\n\nThe wait ends at 8:00 am; the distance remains 17 km.\n\nAt school: 8:35 am, $17+8=25$ km from home.\n\nPlot these points with time on the horizontal axis and distance from home on the vertical axis. Join consecutive points with straight segments; the waiting interval is horizontal.",
